well as syphilis serology. Electroencephalogram, cranial com-
puted tomography (CT) with and without contrast medium,
cranial magnetic resonance imaging (MRI; 1.5 Tesla) with gad-
olinium infusion, and spinal cord MRI were negative. Neuro-
psychological tests showed compromission of language with
dysarthria and dysgraphia, short- and long-term memory dys-
functions, and constructional apraxia. The Mini Mental State
6
score was 17/30. Abdominal echography, thoracic and abdomi-
nal CT, bone marrow biopsy, and right axillary lymphonode
biopsy allowed a diagnosis of immunoblastic non-Hodgkin’s
T-cell lymphoma, IV (B) stage, according to the Non-
Hodgkin’s Lymphoma Classification Project,
7 with thoracic
and abdominal nodal lesions.
